  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given two arrays BBB and DDD, both of length NNN, as well as an integer CCC.\n\nYou also have an array AAA of length NNN **initially filled with zeros**.\n\nYou would like to make the arrays AAA and DDD equal to each other.\n\nTo achieve this, you can perform the following types of moves:\n\n\nCyclic shift the array AAA right one step.\n\nThat is, turn the array AAA from [A1,A2,…,AN][A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_N][A1​,A2​,…,AN​] into [AN,A1,A2,…,AN−1][A_N, A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_{N-1}][AN​,A1​,A2​,…,AN−1​].\n\nThis operation has a cost of CCC.\nChoose an index iii (1≤i≤N1 \\le i \\le N1≤i≤N), and add 111 to AiA_iAi​.\n\nThis operation has a cost of BiB_iBi​.\nEach type of operation can be performed as many times as you like (including 000), and the operations can be performed in any order you like.\n\nFind the **minimum** cost of making the arrays AAA and DDD equal.\n\nIt can be proved that it's always possible to achieve this.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of three lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and CCC — the length of the arrays, and the cost of a cyclic shift.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers B1,…,BNB_1, \\ldots, B_NB1​,…,BN​.\nThe third line contains NNN space-separated integers D1,…,DND_1, \\ldots, D_ND1​,…,DN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the answer: the minimum cost of making arrays AAA and DDD equal.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N≤25001 \\leq N \\leq 25001≤N≤2500",
      "1≤Bi≤1061 \\leq B_i \\leq 10^61≤Bi​≤106",
      "0≤Di≤1060 \\leq D_i \\leq 10^60≤Di​≤106",
      "1≤C≤1061 \\le C \\le 10^61≤C≤106",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 250025002500."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
